From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:29:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: emit JIT code through a writable view and run it
 from an executable view

macOS refuses memory that is writable and executable at once, so Wine keeps
FEX's PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE buffers read-write or read-execute and flips the
page on every fault: each block FEX compiles, links or backpatches costs two
faults and two mprotect calls.

On ARM64EC, FEX's executable memory now comes from one 1 GiB SEC_COMMIT
section (DualView::Init, at process init) mapped twice: a read-write view
that FEX writes, and a read-execute view, marked ARM64EC code with
MEM_EXTENDED_PARAMETER_EC_CODE, that runs. Code addresses are always the
read-execute view's (IsAddressInCodeBuffer, branch targets, cache
maintenance); a store into code goes to ARMEmitter::DualMap::WriteAddr(),
the same address in the read-write view:
- the emitter's buffer (dcn, EmitString, Align) and forward-label binding,
  through a per-buffer write offset that SetBuffer derives from the base, so
  the JIT's temporary heap buffer keeps offset 0;
- the JIT's copy of a compiled block into the code buffer, and of a cached
  one (LoadCachedCode, the code cache's ARM64EC path);
- block linking and delinking (ExitFunctionLink, Direct/IndirectBlockDelinker)
  and the link record's HostCode;
- the unaligned-atomic SIGBUS handler's backpatches and the block tail's
  spin lock it takes.
A code buffer's guard page is no-access in both views. Executable
allocations go through new AllocExec/FreeExec allocator hooks (first fit in
the pool; FreeExec gives a range back with its views' protections, and logs
a protection it couldn't restore); WoW64 keeps RWX memory.

The pool is the one executable code path. DualView::Init failing is fatal
(ERROR_AND_DIE with the NTSTATUS): the platform or Wine's ARM64EC marking of
section views is broken. A full pool is not: the allocation falls back to
RWX memory, which works with W^X flips, and the first such fallback in a
process logs one error with the requested size and the pool's use.

Derived from Madeira (https://github.com/willfaust/FEX.git, branch
ios-port-2607), whose dual-mapped JIT pool on iOS is the map:
- fce78cefd: Buffer's WriteOffset/WritePtr, Bind() through it, block
  linking through DualMap::WriteAddr;
- 61f11e3cc, 6084de076: the PE build's global write offset, the real
  RX-to-RW delta, and NtFlushInstructionCache on the RX address for cache
  maintenance (here ClearICache already reaches it through __clear_cache and
  FEX's FlushInstructionCache);
- 83e12849f, 87b40c220, db4f32768: dispatcher SpillStaticRegs patches written
  through the RW alias. Not taken: they repair an iOS miscompile this build
  doesn't have.
Madeira's pool comes from a debugger-attached JIT region on iOS; here it is
a section, mapped with plain views (no placeholders).

